
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dap): remember attached process names across sessions

The "Attach to PID" prompt kept its history in a register only, so Up
recalled nothing after a restart, and a bare PID never made it into the
history at all.

- The history is saved to `dap-process-history` in the cache directory
  after every attach and loaded when the prompt opens, like the eval
  history (whose load/save helpers now take the register and file).
- A bare PID is remembered by its process's name, since the PID will
  point at nothing, or at something else, by the next session. For a
  Python interpreter that is the script's stem (`worker` for
  `python3 worker.py`, `pytest` for `python3 -m pytest`); otherwise
  `comm`, e.g. `hython-bin`.
- The `languages.toml` note on name lookup no longer claims ambiguous
  names are rejected.
